          "kicker": "Player Departure",
          "heading": "Ireland U20 Star Noah Byrne Departs Leinster For Australian Rules Move",
          "body": "Emerging full-back Noah Byrne has opted to leave Irish rugby, rejecting a professional academy contract with Leinster to pursue a career with the Brisbane Lions in the AFL. The 20-year-old, who started every match for Ireland during this year’s Under-20 Six Nations campaign, was considered one of the most promising back-three prospects in the country. Leinster academy manager Peter Smyth confirmed the move, noting that while the decision is a blow, the province’s door remains open to the talented dual-athlete."
        },
